=== WHAT THE FIRST TWO PASSES OF THIS DRY-RUN REJECTED, before anything was frozen ===
  1. ulpDistance() wrapped to 0 on opposite-sign operands, so control N6 (flip the S_E sign) --
     the largest error the suite can inject -- was scored as a PERFECT MATCH. Reinterpreting two
     doubles as signed integers and subtracting overflows when the signs differ. Fixed with a
     monotonic key; the instrument is now self-tested on planted disagreements (DRYRUN_1B), and a
     non-finite pair poisons the worst-case figures instead of being skipped.
  2. N1 and N2 were run against the reaction sources, which never consult them -- they perturb the
     species index inside the MIXTURE PROPERTY functions only. They looked like dead controls.
     Each control now runs against the criterion it actually controls.
  3. N8 was classified as a control for the BOUNDED q criterion. Omitting the last reaction leaves
     the progress rates untouched (measured 0 in the q bound's units) and changes the
     ACCUMULATION, so it controls the zero-tolerance clause. Same class of error as (2).
  4. THE SUBSTANTIVE ONE. A2's first draft claimed a bounded criterion on q could still reject FMA
     contraction. Measured: contraction moves q by 0.843356 bound-units; the libm difference the
     bound must ADMIT is 3.13865. The contraction effect is SMALLER than the effect the bound has
     to tolerate, so no threshold that lets the correct implementation pass can reject contraction
     on q. That is arithmetic, not a judgement call.

     G9 condition (4) was therefore reallocated to the BITWISE mixture-property criterion, where
     contraction IS visible: 662 of 4096 cells for R_mix and 543 of 4096 for cp_mix. That is
     airtight rather than a consolation, because R_mix, cp_mix and every rate quantity are compiled
     from ONE translation unit carrying ONE --fmad=false property -- the flag cannot be lost for
     the rate path alone without the zero-tolerance criterion failing. DRYRUN_2 asserts both the
     ordering (contraction < libm, the fact that forces the allocation) and the liveness of the
     criterion that now carries the duty.

  5. Recorded, not a defect: FMA cannot reach the omega / S_E accumulation at all. The host's own
     std::fma agrees with multiply-then-add on 12288 of 12288 values, so the products M_i*nu_i*q
     are exactly representable for this mechanism and there is no rounding for a fusion to remove.
     The device control found the same. The accumulation clause's controls are N5, N6 and N8, which
     fire at 3072, 9.4e18 ULP and 4096 values respectively.
